  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: The air quality is expected to be \nunhealthy for sensitive groups early this morning due to smoke\nfrom area wildfires. An Air Quality Alert remains in effect \nthrough 6 AM PDT this morning. \n\nHigh pressure will build across the region through Sunday,\nresulting in a warming trend. Record heat is expected in Ely \nFriday afternoon. Near record heat is anticipated in Elko and \nEureka Friday afternoon. Record heat is expected in Ely Saturday \nafternoon. Near record heat is anticipated in Elko, Winnemucca, \nEureka, and Tonopah Saturday afternoon. Record heat is expected in\nEly Sunday afternoon. Near record heat is anticipated in Eureka \nand Tonopah Sunday afternoon. Heat Advisories will likely be \nrequired for most of the forecast area Friday through Sunday. Here\nare probabilities of triple digit heat for select locations in \nNorthern and Central Nevada on Saturday, August 1st, 2026: \n\nBattle Mountain - 95%\nCarlin - 95%\nElko - 90%\nWinnemucca - 90%\nWest Wendover - 90%\nWells - 90%\nSpring Creek - 80%\nTonopah - 80%\nEly - 75%\nEureka - 75%\n\nHigh temperatures throughout Northern and Central Nevada Monday\nafternoon will be around five degrees above normal for this time\nof year. Maximum temperatures across the forecast area Tuesday\nafternoon will be seven to nine degrees above seasonal values.\nHeat Advisories may be required for parts of Northern and Central\nNevada Monday and Tuesday.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:",
